Title: Diagnosis

Details:
The bug report describes a NullPointerException (NPE) occurring at KMeansPlusPlusClusterer.assignPointsToClusters(KMeansPlusPlusClusterer.java:91). Inspecting the corresponding code for assignPointsToClusters shows:

```java
private static <T extends Clusterable<T>> void
assignPointsToClusters(final Collection<Cluster<T>> clusters, final Collection<T> points) {
    for (final T p : points) {
        Cluster<T> cluster = getNearestCluster(clusters, p);
        cluster.addPoint(p);
    }
}
```

The NPE points to line 91 which corresponds to `cluster.addPoint(p);`. For a null pointer exception here, `cluster` must be null. Thus, getNearestCluster returned null.

Looking at getNearestCluster:

```java
private static <T extends Clusterable<T>> Cluster<T>
getNearestCluster(final Collection<Cluster<T>> clusters, final T point) {
    double minDistance = Double.MAX_VALUE;
    Cluster<T> minCluster = null;
    for (final Cluster<T> c : clusters) {
        final double distance = point.distanceFrom(c.getCenter());
        if (distance < minDistance) {
            minDistance = distance;
            minCluster = c;
        }
    }
    return minCluster;
}
```

getNearestCluster returns null if the clusters collection is empty (for loop never executes, minCluster remains null).

Now, looking at cluster():

```java
public List<Cluster<T>> cluster(final Collection<T> points,
                                final int k, final int maxIterations) {
    List<Cluster<T>> clusters = chooseInitialCenters(points, k, random);
    assignPointsToClusters(clusters, points);
    // iterate updating centers...
}
```

If chooseInitialCenters returns an empty collection, then clusters is empty, and assignPointsToClusters will call getNearestCluster with empty clusters, which will return null, causing NPE.

The test fails when invoking cluster with k=1 on two points. The likely cause is that chooseInitialCenters returns an empty list when it should return one cluster for k=1.

Hence, the root cause is that chooseInitialCenters returns an empty list of clusters under certain inputs, resulting in an empty clusters collection passed into assignPointsToClusters, ultimately causing NPE.

This diagnosis matches the bug description: NPE at assignPointsToClusters due to null cluster returned from getNearestCluster.

Recent bug reports do not seem related to this clustering or initialization problem. Thus, primary evidence points to faulty or missing initialization of clusters in chooseInitialCenters.

The fix should ensure that chooseInitialCenters never returns an empty list if k > 0. The method cluster should handle cases where initial clusters are not properly chosen gracefully or throw an informative exception.

Therefore, the issue occurs because assignPointsToClusters expects a non-empty clusters collection, but it's empty causing null pointer dereference. The root cause is in the initial cluster centers choosing step.

